snp2.6:6.1 starts: Just like a cesspit,
# superseded: snp2.6:6.2 starts: full, used for many years,
# superseded: snp2.6:6.3 starts: one of this sort, befouled,
# superseded: snp2.6:6.4 starts: would be hard to clean.
snp2.7:9.1 starts: Aside from the time
snp2.7:9.2 starts: after menstruation,
snp2.7:9.3 starts: brahmans didn’t engage
snp2.7:9.4 starts: in copulation.
snp2.7:19.1 starts: lavish human wealth,
snp2.7:19.2 starts: surrounded by circles of cows,
snp2.7:19.3 starts: joined with groups of excellent women—
snp2.7:19.4 starts: the brahmans grew greedy.
snp2.7:26.1 starts: Then the king, lord of charioteers,
snp2.7:26.2 starts: induced by the brahmans,
snp2.7:26.3 starts: killed in a sacrifice
snp2.7:26.4 starts: many hundred-thousands of cows.
snp2.7:4.1 starts: They did not despise what was prepared
snp2.7:4.2 starts: food set at doors,
snp2.7:4.3 starts: prepared out of conviction
snp2.7:4.4 starts: for those who seek.
snp2.7:5.1 starts: Prosperous lands & kingdoms
snp2.7:5.2 starts: honored brahmans with multi-colored clothes,
snp2.7:5.3 starts: bedding, & dwellings.
snp2.7:5.4 none
snp2.7:14.1 starts: And in setting up the sacrifice,
snp2.7:14.2 starts: they didn’t harm cows.
snp2.7:14.3 starts: “Like a mother, father,
snp2.7:14.4 starts: or other relative,
snp2.7:14.5 starts: cows are our foremost friends.
snp2.7:14.6 starts: From them comes medicine.
snp2.7:16.1 starts: Delicate, with large bodies,
snp2.7:16.2 starts: beautiful, prestigious,
snp2.7:16.3 starts: brahmans were committed to standards
snp2.7:16.4 starts: of what should & shouldn’t be done
snp2.7:16.5 starts: As long as this lasted in the
snp2.7:16.6 starts: humanity prospered in happiness.
snp2.7:21.1 starts: Then the king, lord of charioteers,
snp2.7:21.2 starts: induced by the brahmans,
snp2.7:21.3 starts: having performed these sacrifices—
snp2.7:21.4 starts: the horse sacrifice, the human sacrifice,
snp2.7:21.5 starts: sammāpāsa, vājapeyya, & niraggaḷa—
snp2.7:21.6 starts: gave the brahmans wealth:
snp2.7:27.1 starts: The cows—
snp2.7:27.2 starts: meek like sheep,
snp2.7:27.3 starts: giving milk by the bucket—
snp2.7:27.4 starts: hadn’t,
snp2.7:27.5 starts: But the king,
snp2.7:27.6 starts: killed them with a knife.
snp2.8:1.1 starts: Because:
snp2.8:1.2 starts: one from whom
snp2.8:1.3 starts: he, learned, honored,
snp2.8:1.4 starts: shows you the Dhamma.
snp2.8:2.1 starts: You, enlightened, heedful,
snp2.8:2.2 starts: practicing the Dhamma
snp2.8:2.3 starts: become
snp2.8:2.4 starts: clear-minded,
snp2.8:3.1 starts: But if you consort with a piddling
snp2.8:3.2 starts: who’s envious,
snp2.8:3.3 starts: you’ll go to death
snp2.8:3.4 starts: with
snp2.8:6.1 starts: But as one who’s embarked
snp2.8:6.2 starts: with rudder & oars,
snp2.8:6.3 starts: would—thoughtful, skillful,
snp2.8:6.4 starts: carry many others across,
